# Every harness dejima supports, and every one under assessment, so a session
# working on this repo can run and test the integration rather than reason
# about it. A harness dejima claims to support and cannot exercise here is one
# whose guards are asserted rather than observed.
#
# claude-code is not listed: like every supported harness it installs from its
# own manifest's `install` spec, into a layer of its own above the base image.
# Nothing here has to name it.
npm:opencode-ai

# Under assessment. Needs AVX2: its CLI is a Bun-embedded compiled binary and
# Bun's default build requires it, so a VM whose CPU model is x86-64-v2-AES -
# Proxmox's default for new guests - gets SIGILL before any output, and no
# baseline build is published. x86-64-v3 or better is the requirement, and is
# what this host now runs. See docs/development.md, "Adding a new harness".
#
# No allowed-domains entry accompanies this, unlike opencode: Cline fetches no
# provider catalogue at startup. Its own hosted endpoints (api.cline.bot,
# app.cline.bot, otel.cline.bot) are deliberately absent for the same reason
# the model API is - a name granted by being written here is a name nobody
# reviewed, and the point of assessing Cline is to point it at an endpoint of
# our choosing.
npm:cline

apt:tmux
apt:bats
